prompt Take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first on the road ahead (1024-round itinerary, six-season double-seat, Rye-first crypto parity wave); Rye prioritized, Glow on green-witnessed Rye, send often as signed rounds, stop only at custody gates.
think Walked REMEMBER + the three design docs. The active track is Season G's Monocypher-parity wave — eighteen source-parity rungs landed, the last two Elligator 2 and dirty X25519. The prior session log named the exact next crux: crypto_elligator_key_pair, composing dirty_small + elligator rev + a chacha20-seeded retry loop into a hidden keypair. It is the highest-Lindy tractable rung — it closes the key-hiding family end to end and is the key Comlink's obfuscated first packet carries — and it is gate-free, purely local, Rye-first.
think Read Monocypher's crypto_elligator_key_pair: a 64-byte buffer whose high half seeds ChaCha20-djb (key=high half, counter 0, zero nonce), the low half becoming a candidate secret and the high half a fresh value; take crypto_x25519_dirty_fast of the low half; try crypto_elligator_rev under the high half's first byte as tweak; loop while unrepresentable, the failed try's fresh ChaCha bytes seeding the next. On success the representative overwrites the high half. Reproduced the loop step for step over our GREEN dirty_small (== dirty_fast byte-for-byte) and elligator.rev.
think The one clean reuse: Monocypher calls ChaCha20-DJB (8-byte nonce, 64-bit counter); our chacha20.rye is IETF (12-byte nonce, 32-bit counter). At counter 0 with an all-zero nonce the two state layouts COINCIDE — words 12..15 are zero either way — so a single 64-byte block is byte-identical. Documented as an invariant and PROVEN by the parity witness (which links the real DJB call), not merely asserted in a comment.
obs Byte-for-byte GREEN on the first parity run: our key_pair equals Monocypher's crypto_elligator_key_pair over sixteen seeds on BOTH the secret key and the representative (thirty-two lines). The selftest adds an internal proof no external vector gives — the composition is CLOSED: map(hidden) == dirty_small(secret) across twenty-four seeds, so the two halves of the result truly belong together. Bounded the retry loop at a named maximum (64, ~2^-64 exhaustion) with a named error rather than an unbounded wait.
obs New crypto/*.rye module tripped the count guard bijection. Registered the module witness in the suite and bumped the narration 59→60 files, twenty-one→twenty-two compositions (a composition, not a primitive — it authors no new arithmetic). Count guard GREEN at 60; crypto/README.md + docs/CRYPTO.md each gained the rung row and synced counts, same round (docs-implementation-sync). TAME style check clean.
